   "format": "mcq",
   "stem": {
      "text": "The functions \\( f \\), \\( g \\), and \\( h \\) are continuous for all real numbers, with \\( f(0) = 4 \\), \\( f(1) = 2 \\), \\( f(2) = 3 \\), \\( f(3) = 1 \\), \\( f(4) = 3 \\), \\( g(0) = 2 \\), \\( g(1) = 1 \\), \\( g(2) = 2 \\), \\( g(3) = 2 \\), \\( g(4) = 2 \\), \\( h(0) = 3 \\), \\( h(1) = 1 \\), \\( h(2) = 0 \\), \\( h(3) = 1 \\), \\( h(4) = 0 \\). Find the value of \\( \\lim_{x \\to 3} \\left[ 3g(h(x)) - 2f(g(x)) + h(f(x)) \\right] \\)."
   },
   "answer_key": {
      "form": "symbolic",
      "mathjson": -2
   },
   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "Each function is continuous, so each limit at 3 is a function value: \\( f(3) = 1 \\), \\( g(3) = 2 \\), \\( h(3) = 1 \\).",
         "mathjson": 1
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "The expression is a sum of constant multiples of three composites. In each composite the outer function is continuous at the limit of the inner one, so \\( \\lim_{x \\to 3} g(h(x)) = g(1) = 1 \\), \\( \\lim_{x \\to 3} f(g(x)) = f(2) = 3 \\), \\( \\lim_{x \\to 3} h(f(x)) = h(1) = 1 \\).",
         "mathjson": 1
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "Apply the sum and constant multiple theorems: \\( (3)(1) + (-2)(3) + (1)(1) = -2 \\).",
         "mathjson": -2
      }
   ],
